  "task": {
    "source_message_id": 887,
    "speaker": "client",
    "text": "Thanks, Luka. Everything is clear:\n1. For v4, leave VRTC NC because this board has no external RTC chip. On the RTC topic, I realized that I previously mixed up VRTC with VBACKUP. VBACKUP (pin 27) supplies backup power to keep the AXP2101's internal RTC running after the main battery is removed. Could you expose VBACKUP on a small test pad or via beside PWROK from item #10? This would let us later install a 200 µF capacitor for \\~8-10 min of hot-swap tolerance, a supercap for several weeks, or a CR1220 coin cell for \\~9 years of real time-keeping. Nothing needs to be populated now; only expose the pad.\n2. For the buttons (R16/R17/R18), agreed: convert all three to pull-ups at 3V3. They remain active LOW, with connector pin 1 tied to GND and a press shorting the GPIO input to GND. I updated <http://board-package.example|pcb-integrated.md> to reflect this.\n3. The PIR (R19) and Touch (R20/R25) circuits are already correct as pull-downs and need no changes. Both the AM312 (PIR) and TTP223 (touch) provide push-pull active-HIGH outputs, so their internal drivers override the 20 k pull-down while active. The pull-down to GND simply ensures a defined LOW state whenever a sensor is unplugged."
  },
